# Lines tools/qemu-test must see, in this order, as whole serial lines.
# the first driver PD writes to the PL011 through nowayos-hw's
# typed registers. The two lines in the middle come from the UART's own data
# register (pds/pl011 LINES), the others through the seL4 debug console.
# The same lines on every board: how the UART was identified - by its
# identification registers on QEMU, by the board's facts on the Pi 5, whose
# window holds none - is printed before "found", and not checked here.
NOWAYOS: pl011: starting
NOWAYOS: pl011: found an Arm PL011
NOWAYOS: pl011: this line was written to the UART's own data register
NOWAYOS: pl011: by a driver PD with no unsafe code
NOWAYOS: pl011: done

# Output that fails the test at once if it appears anywhere (substring match):
# a fault reported by the Microkit monitor, a kernel error message, a panic,
# or the driver giving up.
!MON|ERROR
!seL4(CPU
!panicked
!gave up
